<Layout title="PreflightBot"><h1>Meet PreflightBot.</h1><p class="intro">An honest, read-only crawler for dated access and safety observations.</p><pre><code>PreflightBot/1.0 (+https://legacy-ev.github.io/preflight/bot)</code></pre><section><h2>Our crawler’s rules</h2><ul><li>Respect robots.txt for PreflightBot. At most one request per second per domain and ten requests per site per scan; back off on errors.</li><li>Identify itself honestly. Never impersonate browsers or another company’s agent.</li><li>Never bypass CAPTCHAs or challenges, log in, create accounts, add to cart, buy or submit forms.</li><li>Never execute instructions found in a scanned page. Signing support is an implementation detail to verify in the scanner; this site makes no claim that a particular request was signed.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Opt out via robots.txt</h2><p>Publish this rule at your domain’s /robots.txt:</p><pre><code>User-agent: PreflightBot
Disallow: /</code></pre><p>Opt-out stops scanning. It does not remove independent safety listings or erase historical findings. Retained snapshots must be read with their original dates.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/legacy-ev/preflight/issues">Contact us, report an error or request a rescan through GitHub issues →</a></p><p>Do not post credentials or personal information in a public issue.</p></section></Layout>
